  "goodToKnow": "Das Erdgas is natural gas, and das Erdöl is crude oil. Before 2022, Germany got over half of its gas from Russia, much of it through the Nord Stream pipelines. After Russia's invasion of Ukraine, deliveries stopped, and Germany built its first LNG (Flüssigerdgas) terminals in record time, starting at Wilhelmshaven in December 2022. Many German homes still heat with gas. It has no plural."
